# LEGACY / UNUSED — not consumed by anything in this repo.
#
# The real source of truth for runtime dependencies is pyproject.toml +
# uv.lock. install/requirements.txt is autogenerated FROM those via:
#   uv export --format requirements.txt --no-dev --no-emit-project --output-file install/requirements.txt
# (see install/requirements.txt's own header, and
# scripts/checks/check_requirements_drift.sh, which is what CI enforces).
#
# Do NOT edit this file expecting it to affect requirements.txt — running
# the pip-compile command this file used to suggest produces a
# requirements.txt that the drift check then rejects. To add/upgrade a
# dependency, edit pyproject.toml's [project.dependencies], run
# `uv lock` (or `uv lock --upgrade-package <name>`), then the `uv export`
# command above.
#
# Packages with sys_platform guards are only installed on Linux (Pi).

